ship:
  name: Henri IV
  index: PFSC110
  tier: 10
  class: cruiser
  nation: France
  group: upgradeable
  category: tech_tree
  status: released
explanation: "Damage saturation: a ship's HP is split among hull sections (bow, stern, casemate or midsection, superstructure, auxiliary rooms, citadel), each with its own HP pool, plus a hull pool of 75% of ship HP that has no geometry of its own. A penetrating hit drains the pool of the section it damages and, for a section that lists drains, the hull pool too; overpenetrations, fire and flooding drain only ship HP. penetration_damage_pct is the share of an AP shell's listed damage a penetrating hit deals there while the pools it drains have HP: 33% on most sections, half from each pool, and 100% on the citadel. Once a section's own pool is spent it is saturated (black in the damage model) and penetrations there deal only saturated_damage_pct, half as much. Once the hull pool is spent, every section that drains it counts as saturated and penetrations deal 10% (Wargaming wiki). The citadel never saturates, and neither does the midsection of most destroyers, which always takes its full 33%. Repair Party restores up to repairable_pct of the damage a section has taken (Halland's unique upgrade raises it on every section but the citadel), and its healing refills every section's pool in proportion to what that section has lost, so a healed section takes its full share again. French battleships and cruisers have no special saturation: their sections follow the same rules as those of other nations. \"French saturation\" is a destroyer trait: the midsection of most French destroyers (not Aigle or Kleber TE) and of a few others, such as Shigure and Blyskawica '52, has a pool that saturates, so past that much damage there they take half damage instead of full damage."
